AP64350 official PSpice transient model - ngspice compatibility check only
* Purpose: does the vendor model run in ngspice 47 and regulate 8.4 V -> 5 V?
* This is NOT the HAT Rev A design and NOT a validation of AP64501/PAM8406.
* Vendor file: Diodes AP64350_SO-8EP.zip, ap64350_patched.lib, Model Version 1.0,
* 2021-10-14, datasheet DS41976 Rev.5-2, built in PSpice 17.2 (Allegro).
* Subcircuit pin order: BST VIN EN RT_CLK FB COMP GND SW (not package pins).
.include "C:/Users/yilv/AppData/Local/duck-robot-tools/models/diodes/AP64350/ap64350_patched.lib"

VIN  vin 0 DC 8.4
CIN  vin 0 10u

XU1  bst vin en rt fb comp 0 sw AP64350

L1   sw vout 4.7u
RESR vout cx 5m
COUT cx 0 47u
CBST sw bst 0.1u

RTOP vout fb 52.3k
RBOT fb 0 10k

RC   comp cc 10k
CC   cc 0 4.7n
CP   comp 0 100p

REN  vin en 100k
RT   rt 0 100k

* Load: 0.5 A, step to 3.5 A at 1.45 ms
ILOAD vout 0 PWL(0 0.5 1.4m 0.5 1.45m 3.5 2.4m 3.5)

.options rshunt=1e9 reltol=1e-2
.tran 0.5u 2.5m
.meas tran vout_avg AVG V(vout) FROM=2.2m TO=2.4m
.meas tran vout_min MIN V(vout) FROM=2.2m TO=2.4m
.meas tran vout_max MAX V(vout) FROM=2.2m TO=2.4m
.meas tran vout_dip MIN V(vout) FROM=1.4m TO=1.9m
.end


